  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has baked NNN cakes, each weighing XXX kilograms. Now, he needs to deliver them.\n\nHe has many vehicles, that he will use to transport the cakes. Each vehicle can carry at most YYY kilograms of cake. It is guaranteed that Y≥XY \\ge XY≥X, so each vehicle can carry at least 111 cake.\n\nHow many vehicles will Chef need to transport all the cakes?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of each test case contains 333 integers - N,XN, XN,X and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput on a new line the minimum number of vehicles Chef will need.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤101 \\le N \\le 101≤N≤10",
      "1≤X≤Y≤101 \\le X \\le Y \\le 101≤X≤Y≤10"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6 4 6",
        "output": "6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nEach vehicle can only fit 111 cake, and thus Chef will need 666 vehicles for 666 cakes."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4 1 3",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef can put 222 cakes in each of the 222 vehicles."
      }
    ]
  },
